{"name":"Bronze Treasure","hex":"#b08d57","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bronze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring or man-made alloy of copper, usually in combination with tin, but also with one or more other metals.","A reddish-brown colour, the colour of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of bronze metal.","Having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze"},{"term":"treasure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A collection of valuable things; accumulated wealth; a stock of money, jewels, etc.","Anything greatly valued.\n\nA term of endearment.\n\n The female genitals; pudenda."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider to be precious; to value highly.","To store or stow in a safe place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, ductility, or machinability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg/330px-Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze","wikidata":"Q34095"},{"title":"Treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure is a concentration of wealth — often originating from ancient history — that is considered lost and/or forgotten until rediscovered. Some jurisdictions legally define what constitutes treasure, such as in the British Treasure Act 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=e